+# Bounded hot-cache restart feasibility probe
+
+This is an isolated native experiment, not production wiring. Base native source
+is `cc8367a1076b6245574f209c7d007118cf9016b1`; link the matching qualified
+`librocksdbjni-linux64.so` (SHA256
+`18d5865e39cccede36d63146eb9037837b423199930504e3730d2d91d9ff6214`).
+The image's older standalone librocksdb is ABI incompatible with these headers
+and was rejected after a fixture crash. Build uses the image only as a compiler
+container; no packaged JNI artifact is modified.
+
+Run `build.sh SOURCE CANDIDATE OUTPUT` inside
+`codex-paired-compaction-qualified-build-cache:20261011`, with at most 3 CPUs and
+8 GiB, then `python3 test.py OUTPUT/probe OUTPUT`. Each test opens a separate
+process and verifies actual values from both column families. The C ABI in
+`probe.h` keeps all C++ object ownership inside one call. A Java 25 FFM caller
+needs only strings, scalar values, and an output buffer.
+
+The cache is one 16 MiB HyperClock cache for DATA and METADATA. A bounded registry
+retains up to 4096 latest Insert/Lookup keys. Capture performs primary-only lookup,
+serializes supported resident entries, and filters stable SST key prefixes from
+all live column families. Handles are released before disk writes. Basic helpers
+on previously restored blocks are recovered through role plus deleter identity.
+On SSD, an immutable snapshot retains only offsets/keys in its RAM index; values
+are read on demand. Serialized bytes have `kVolatileTier` source even on SSD:
+`cache/typed_cache.h` requires this for already-serialized primary objects.
+
+Format v1 is intentionally specific to x86 little-endian RocksDB 11.8.1 and the
+matched native build, with an 8-byte build-family magic, format version, count,
+bounded per-record lengths and CRC32C over lengths, role, key and value. Files
+are capped at 64 MiB, blocks at 1 MiB. All records validate before activation;
+lookup rechecks CRC before deserialization. Missing or invalid snapshots are
+misses. Unique temporary files, file fsync, atomic rename, and directory fsync
+publish a generation. Test-only `RSHC_TEST_FAIL_BEFORE_RENAME` injects a failure
+which preserves the previous generation; stale temporary names do not block
+subsequent capture. Calls sharing paths must be serialized.
+
+Observed mechanism: 2048 verified Gets in each process, with 488 restored blocks
+(484 DATA and 4 INDEX/FILTER metadata); 2,006,192-byte snapshots survive capture,
+restart, recapture and another restart. Tests cover absent snapshots, byte caps,
+checksum corruption, truncation, invalid lengths/version, failed publication,
+and recovery. IO_uring is unavailable in the Docker test and falls back to POSIX.
+
+Limits: this fixture proves no HDD latency/throughput improvement. Observation
+is aggregate across CFs; equal per-CF capture coverage is not established.
+Insert includes startup/build activity, and pinned accesses bypass Lookup, so it
+is not a faithful foreground hotness ranking. Ambiguous OtherBlock roles,
+including dictionaries, are excluded. There is no cancellation/time/I/O budget,
+separate DATA/METADATA quota, background concurrency stress, compaction replacement
+test, or production API yet. Capture buffers the bounded generation in RAM and
+startup scans/checksums its payload before retaining the index, so cost scales
+with the configured cap. Hard process crashes can leave owned temporary files;
+scoped retention/cleanup remains future work. CRC is corruption detection, not
+an adversarial authentication scheme.
diff --git a/experiments/hot_cache/build.sh b/experiments/hot_cache/build.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..e2cdf28
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/hot_cache/build.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+# Run in qualified Docker image with <=3 CPUs/8GiB. Source is exact cc8367a
+# experiment checkout, runtime is the already-qualified cc8367a native artifact.
+source_root=${1:?source checkout}
+candidate=${2:?exact native candidate directory}
+output=${3:?owned output directory}
+mkdir -p "$output"
+cp "$candidate/librocksdbjni-linux64.so" "$output/"
+flags=(-std=c++20 -O1 -g -DROCKSDB_PLATFORM_POSIX -DROCKSDB_LIB_IO_POSIX -DROCKSDB_USE_RTTI -I"$source_root" -I"$source_root/include")
+g++-12 "${flags[@]}" -fPIC -shared "$source_root/experiments/hot_cache/probe.cc" -L"$output" -lrocksdbjni-linux64 '-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN' -o "$output/libhot_cache_probe.so"
+g++-12 "${flags[@]}" -DRSHC_MAIN "$source_root/experiments/hot_cache/probe.cc" -L"$output" -lrocksdbjni-linux64 '-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN' -o "$output/probe"
+sha256sum "$output/librocksdbjni-linux64.so" "$output/libhot_cache_probe.so"
